# Configuration for the local LLM server. Sourced by every script, so it is
# plain shell — no quotes needed unless a value contains spaces.
#
# Precedence: built-in defaults  <  this file  <  environment variables.
# So `LLM_PORT=9090 llm on` overrides whatever is set here.
#
# That precedence is why every assignment below uses ${VAR:=default} rather
# than VAR=default. A bare assignment would overwrite a value that was already
# set in the environment, which silently makes this file unbeatable. If you add
# a setting here, use the same form.
#
# After editing, restart the server for changes to take effect:
#     llm restart

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- network --
# Address to bind. Defaults to the detected LAN address; 127.0.0.1 makes it
# reachable only through an SSH tunnel. Do not use 0.0.0.0 unless you really
# mean to expose it, and remember there is no API key.
#: "${LLM_HOST:=127.0.0.1}"
: "${LLM_PORT:=8080}"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ model --
# Context length. KV cache costs roughly 17 MiB per 1024 tokens for
# Qwen3.5-9B at q8_0, and it does not slow decode — it only costs prefill time
# on very long prompts. Verified to load at 16384 (272 MiB) / 24576 (408 MiB) /
# 32768 (544 MiB) on an RX 6600 (8 GB). Larger values will fail to load on
# smaller cards; the failure is an out-of-memory error at startup, not a
# slowdown.
#
# 32768 is the default because agentic clients such as OpenCode need it: their
# own system prompt and tool definitions run ~6.6k tokens, which at 16384
# leaves almost no room for the conversation. Use 16384 if you are only calling
# this from scripts, or if your card has less than 8 GB.
#: "${LLM_CTX:=32768}"

# CPU threads. Decode is memory-bandwidth-bound, so more threads than physical
# cores rarely helps.
#: "${LLM_THREADS:=6}"

# GPU layers. 99 means "offload everything possible" and is what you want.
# Lower values collapse decode speed, because the GPU is doing the work.
#: "${LLM_NGL:=99}"

# --------------------------------------------------------------- plumbing --
# Group owning /dev/dri/renderD*. Usually "render"; "video" on some systems.
#: "${LLM_RENDER_GROUP_NAME:=render}"

# tmux session name, so you can run two instances side by side.
#: "${LLM_SESSION:=llm}"
